    "result": "Excellent! All tests now pass. Here's a summary of the fixes:\n\n## Issues Fixed\n\n**1. Missing named export in `/src/finetune/index.js`**\n   - The test was importing `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export, but it was only available through the default export\n   - Fixed by adding a named export statement for `APPROVAL_STATUSES` and other constants\n\n**2. Wrong function signature in `/src/eval/metrics.js`**\n   - The `toxicityMetric` function had signature `(outputs, bannedTerms = defaultBannedTerms)`, but `runEvaluations` calls all metrics with `(outputs, references)`\n   - When `references` was passed as the second argument, it was treated as `bannedTerms`, causing toxicity checks to fail unexpectedly\n   - Fixed by updating the signature to `(outputs, references, bannedTerms = defaultBannedTerms)` to match the calling convention, with `references` parameter accepted but unused\n\nAll 28 tests now pass across all 8 test files. The public API exports remain unchanged.",
